{
 "comment": "clause44: the client's money categories. Interest to a bank goes to the exempt column and bank charges to 'other than composition' whatever the lender's GSTIN (the module check leaves both out); a charge on a journal with no party is 'no party' (a reason comes before a forced column); a ledger in both the bank-charge category and the no-supplier list is 'no supplier'; interest to an individual lender keeps the ordinary rule (no GSTIN: unregistered; a GSTIN and no tax: exempt) and raises the judgement finding, including a line on a ledger that is also a depreciation ledger; a depreciation ledger is a depreciation entry even when its category is a judgement one; partner remuneration (also on the no-supplier list) and a mixed interest-and-charges ledger are judgement items outside the columns; an unrecognised category and a padded one change nothing. Every GSTIN is invented (fourteenth character Y).",
